  "body": "Follow-up to #54 (PR #210). The wrap now refuses by name a non-turned feature (flat, keyway, cross hole) that crosses its seam, because reshaping the clearing area around a ragged seam still left a gouge band at the feature's end stations. The user has to rotate the work so the feature clears the seam.\n\nDone means: the wrap picks its seam angle itself, at an angle where every station is turned (no feature facets straddle it), so a D-flat bar wraps whatever its placement. It refuses by name only when no such angle exists (a feature all the way round). Pin: the rotary_dflat placements that are refused today wrap, with 0 cut tips inside the true cross-section.",
